sequenceDiagram
  %% Record-only attachment: recorded Process intent, no Node execution.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:node-service:attach
  %% kind: instance.node_service_attach
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  Note over CLI: Resolve command inputs
  alt local input refused
    CLI--xCLI: Invalid input or cancelled<br/>No attach request
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - instance.id_invalid refuses an invalid supplied or missing noninteractive Instance ID, or an empty Instance list after the registry GET; no mutation request is sent.
    %%> - instance.node_service_process_required refuses a missing noninteractive Process ID, or an empty Node Process list after its registry GET; no mutation request is sent.
    %%> - instance.node_service_host_key_required and instance.node_service_port_key_required refuse omitted key names only in JSON or noninteractive mode.
    %%> - validation.failed refuses an invalid supplied Process ID or port, including an explicitly empty port.
    %%> - input.cancelled ends a cancelled terminal selection or text prompt before mutation.
    %%> - State stays unchanged. Invalid supplied IDs or port and missing noninteractive inputs send no request. Terminal cancellation or empty choices can follow registry reads.
  else local input available
    opt human terminal needs input
      CLI->>GW: Read registry choices
      GW-->>CLI: Registry choices
      Note over CLI: Select IDs and enter keys
      %%> When:
      %%> - Omitted IDs use registry data lists; omitted environment keys use validated text prompts. Reads may refuse without an attachment change.
    end
    CLI->>GW: instance:node-service<br/>attach INSTANCE --process=PROCESS
    %%> Command:
    %%> - orbit instance:node-service:attach INSTANCE --process=PROCESS --host-env-key=KEY --port-env-key=KEY
    %%> - syntax: instance:node-service:attach
    Note over GW: Check request and access
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - peer.identity_unknown, node_access.required or http.404 refuses the caller or numeric Instance; authority is required for both the Instance Node and selected Process Node.
    %%> - validation.failed refuses invalid body fields or environment keys.
    alt request refused
      GW--xCLI: Named refusal<br/>No attachment change
    else request admitted
      Note over GW: Lock and check Instance
      alt busy or container runtime
        GW--xCLI: Instance refused<br/>No attachment change
        %%> On failure:
        %%> - instance.lifecycle_busy refuses an inactive Instance, running migration or detach.
        %%> - instance.node_service_runtime_unsupported refuses an existing container runtime.
      else checkout available
        Note over GW: Check standalone Process<br/>and TCP publication
        %%> Why:
        %%> - Admission uses recorded ownership, desired state and Docker publication; it contacts no Node.
        alt Process or endpoint refused
          GW--xCLI: Target refused<br/>No attachment change
          %%> On failure:
          %%> - instance.node_service_process_missing and instance.node_service_process_owned refuse an unknown, non-Node or service-owned Process; remote Docker Processes are eligible.
          %%> - instance.node_service_protocol_unsupported and instance.node_service_process_stopped refuse non-TCP or desired-stopped targets.
          %%> - instance.node_service_port_required and instance.node_service_port_unpublished refuse an omitted choice among several ports or an unpublished TCP host port.
          %%> - instance.node_service_port_reserved, instance.host_unavailable and instance.node_service_listener_private refuse infrastructure ports, a missing Instance bridge, or an ineligible bind. A remote target needs exactly one TCP publication at its owner's private IPv4 WireGuard address.
          %%> - instance.dev_band_reserved refuses a same-Node target in the development band, 5173-5199
        else valid endpoint
          alt identical attachment
            GW-->>CLI: Already attached<br/>changed false, reason code
            %%> When:
            %%> - The Process, port and both keys match the existing record; its stable skip reason is instance.node_service_target_unchanged.
          else environment key conflict
            GW--xCLI: Key conflict<br/>No attachment change
            %%> On failure:
            %%> - instance.node_service_environment_conflict requires detaching the old record before a correction.
          else unused keys
            Note over GW: Record service Node<br/>and attachment
            alt transaction fails
              GW--xCLI: Transaction failed<br/>Attachment write rolls back
            else transaction commits
              GW-->>CLI: Target result<br/>changed true, request ID
            end
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
